Did you try giving the whole box to the robot?

Did you train the robot to copy the 365?

Did you drop the copy of the 365 on the 0?

Did you train the robot to copy the 1 and drop it on the 0 next
to the scale?

Did you press 'Escape' to finish training the robot?

Did you give the robot the box?

Did you use Dusty to remove the two zeros from the box in the robot's
thought bubble?

It is sometimes easier to vacuum out the whole box from a robot's
thought bubble, spit it out, and then change it and finally put
it back in the robot's thought bubble.

Well, what I would do is to give the whole box to the robot.  Then
I'd have the robot copy the 365 and drop it on the last zero.  Then
I'd copy the 1 and drop it on the other 0.  Then I'd press 'Escape'.  I'd
give the box to the robot and wait for Dusty to appear.  Then I'd vacuum
away the two zeros from his thought bubble.  Then I'd give the box
back to the robot and wait.


